  "reading_notes": {
    "delta_comp": "delta_comp is 0 on both paths at every generation: with m <= d the key columns stay numerically independent even when they are 0.999 aligned, so pinv(K)K = I and the residual vanishes. It is the wrong discriminator when the store is wider than it is occupied; the key spectrum (top_share, effective_rank) and the read margin are the discriminators here. This is a reading, not a pass",
    "margin_decay": "repaired median margin decays 0.0686 -> 0.0584 -> 0.0303 -> 0.0200 while occupancy goes 8 -> 16 -> 32 -> 64 in d=128; it reaches the 0.02 growth threshold at generation 4, so growth adds directions but each added key buys less separation as occupancy approaches d/2"
  },
  "decision": "pass",
  "failure": null,
  "what_pass_means": "on this synthetic fixture, capacity can be doubled four times while keeping the reserve, without dropping or evicting a single write, and every newly written key sits in the relatedness band relative to the subspace already present",
